 is one appointment; repeat patients remain repeat appointments.", "UTC calendar dates are compared because the appointment field has no meaningful visit time.", "Quarantine negative age and booking-after-appointment dates; preserve other source records.", "No-show is Yes = missed, No = attended. Rates are missed / appointments, recomputed from additive counts.", "SMS groups are observational and differ in booking lead time. Their difference is not an estimate of message effectiveness.", "The planning control applies an assumed relative reduction in missed appointments; it is not a measured intervention result."], "evidenceFlow": [{"title": "Download pinned public source", "detail": "https://www.kaggle.com/api/v1/datasets/download/joniarroba/noshowappointments"}, {"title": "Verify archive SHA-256", "detail": "4b4f258837029bd4e61ed4c9bab2ce8a3b8a299d1a4f5bdabcc98967d5e29a43"}, {"title": "Reproduce", "detail": "Run python pipeline.py, then the executed analysis.ipynb companion."}], "sql": "-- One row per appointment date, waiting-time band and recorded SMS indicator.\n-- Input is validated by pipeline.py; all measures are additive counts.\nSELECT appointment_date, weekday, lead_band, sms_received,\n       COUNT(*) AS appointments,\n       SUM(no_show) AS missed,\n       SUM(lead_days) AS total_lead_days\nFROM appointments\nGROUP BY appointment_date, weekday, lead_band, sms_received\nORDER BY appointment_date, lead_band, sms_received;\n", "metricDefinitions": [{"label": "Missed appointment rate", "definition": "Sum of missed appointments divided by sum of appointments in the selected cohorts; Yes in No-show means missed."}, {"label": "Booking lead time", "definition": "Appointment calendar date minus scheduling calendar date, in days."}, {"label": "Scenario recovered appointments", "definition": "Observed missed appointments multiplied by an assumed relative reduction. Scenario only; no intervention effect is measured."}]}}, "quality": {"rows": [{"source_rows": 110527, "accepted_rows": 110521, "quarantined_rows": 6, "negative_age_rows": 1, "negative_lead_rows": 5, "age_above_110_rows": 5, "missing_values": 0, "duplicate_appointment_ids": 0, "unique_patients": 62299, "start": "2016-04-29", "end": "2016-06-08", "sha256": "4b4f258837029bd4e61ed4c9bab2ce8a3b8a299d1a4f5bdabcc98967d5e29a43", "missed": 22314, "attendance_rate": 0.7981017182254956, "no_show_rate": 0.2018982817745044, "mean_lead_days": 10.184345056595578}], "source": {"label": "Source validation report", "provider": "Kaggle", "url": "https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/joniarroba/noshowappointments", "files": ["KaggleV2-May-2016.csv"], "classification": "Historical observations, Brazil, 2016", "notes": ["Joni Hoppen and Aquarela Analytics", "CC BY-NC-SA 4.0", "Each row is one appointment; repeat patients remain repeat appointments.", "UTC calendar dates are compared because the appointment field has no meaningful visit time.", "Quarantine negative age and booking-after-appointment dates; preserve other source records.", "No-show is Yes = missed, No = attended. Rates are missed / appointments, recomputed from additive counts.", "SMS groups are observational and differ in booking lead time. Their difference is not an estimate of message effectiveness.", "The planning control applies an assumed relative reduction in missed appointments; it is not a measured intervention result."], "evidenceFlow": [{"title": "Download pinned public source", "detail": "https://www.kaggle.com/api/v1/datasets/download/joniarroba/noshowappointments"}, {"title": "Verify archive SHA-256", "detail": "4b4f258837029bd4e61ed4c9bab2ce8a3b8a299d1a4f5bdabcc98967d5e29a43"}, {"title": "Reproduce", "detail": "Run python pipeline.py, then the executed analysis.ipynb companion."}]}}}}